===Numeral===
{{head|en|numeral}}

# {{cln|en|cardinal numbers}} A [[numerical]] [[value]] equal to [[9]]; the number following [[eight]] and preceding [[ten]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=Thomas Mchenry|title=Along the Rails: A Juror's Journey|page=85|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=4HaXkJscauQC&pg=PA85&dq=%22the+whole+nine+yards%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=io8qU63JCcTQkwXu_IGIBA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22the%20whole%20nine%20yards%22&f=false|passage=Would they want me to vote my conscience or would they want us to unanimously go the whole '''nine''' yards, declare him sane and possibly have the trial end up in a death sentence?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Eoin McSweeney|title=As Covid-19 cases rise in Nigeria, a government policy is creating crowds and chaos|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/10/africa/nigeria-national-identification-numbers-covid-intl/index.html|date=2021-02-10|passage=Tamunowari Tetenta, a 20-year-old mechanical engineering student, says he has attempted to register for his NIN on '''nine''' different occasions in Port Harcourt, a city southeast of Lagos.}}
# {{n-g|Describing a [[group]] or [[set]] with nine [[element]]s.}}
#: {{ux|en|A cat has '''nine''' lives.}}

